## Task

Apply the task above to the workspace. Prefer installed skills'
script APIs for build/test verbs — read the linked SKILL.md files
first to learn the exact command surface. Fall back to the raw
commands only when no matching skill exists.

Make only changes directly required by the assigned task; no
speculative helpers, abstractions, or defensive code for
hypothetical scenarios.

Report honestly via `applied`: set `applied=true` ONLY when every
acceptance criterion is met and the build/tests you were instructed
to run pass. If you ran out of budget, hit an unresolvable blocker,
or delivered a partial change, set `applied=false` and put the
reason in `error` — the pool loop will retry or skip the task per
its retry policy. Do NOT weaken criteria to claim success.

Record every command or skill invocation actually run into
`cmds_used` — this list is reviewed to prevent gaming the
verify-tests gate by hand-rolling a command that bypasses an
available skill shim.

## Output

```bash
LOOM=~/.kiro/skills/home/loomv2/scripts/loom.sh
$LOOM output init "{{ input.__loom.workdir }}" --task '{{ input.__task.id }}'
$LOOM output add  "{{ input.__loom.workdir }}" --task '{{ input.__task.id }}' \
    --set applied=true \
    --set-json 'error=""' \
    --set diff='<unified diff>' \
    --set 'files_changed[]=<path>' \
    --set notes='<notes markdown>' \
    --set 'cmds_used[]=<command or skill invocation>'
```

On a failed/partial round, instead set:

```bash
$LOOM output add "{{ input.__loom.workdir }}" --task '{{ input.__task.id }}' \
    --set applied=false \
    --set error='<why the task could not be completed>' \
    --set diff='<unified diff of whatever was changed, or empty>' \
    --set-json 'files_changed=[]' \
    --set notes='<notes markdown>' \
    --set 'cmds_used[]=<command or skill invocation>'
```
